 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "West Wind, bring to us a delicate wind\nFrom the boundless deeps of the ages gone,\nAnd with it let our hearts be confident\nOf what shall come and when; enough,\nEnough we marvel at eternity,\nTo find no end.  When Time shall break away\nThe watch that waits for all mankind,\nThat was made for us, finally,\nHis servant is still serving us again.\nEast Wind, year by year, so rare alone\nShall we know him as thou wonders\nOf many years have ever",
